A||N||10||ur2biteme||swaping an '88 duke into an '87||||1||
Z||000000||ur2biteme||09-04-2001||05:00 AM||||hi guys.  havent been on here in a while.  hopefully you can help.  i've spent the last 2 hours searching the archives trying to find some insight on this.<P>my engine has developed a rather loud knock.  i want to say it's a rod.  i'm looking for a replacement engine and i've come across a couple 88's.  i heard a while back that the differences are relatively minor, and that they bolt up and work relatively the same regardless, but i've heard recently that there's more to it than just 'plug and play'.  any insight and/or mentionings of parts and modifications needed would be of great help.  <P>thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||ChadMan||09-04-2001||08:51 AM||||Ed Parks told me the 87 and 88 Dukes (distributorless) are easily interchangeable and use the same mounts, wiring harnesses, etc.  The only difference is the balance shaft/oil filter assembly in the pan on the 88 - but that won't affect installation at all.<P>Good luck...||||reg||1
Z||000002||Raydar||09-04-2001||09:16 AM||||I have heard exactly the same thing. All the mounts and electrics should be the same. I've even heard (never verified) that some of the late 87s might have even gotten the 88 motor, with the internal balancers. <BR>While you have it removed, do yourself a favor and install the V-6 tranny mounts. See Ogre's cave, at the top of the page, for details.<P><BR>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT><BR><p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 09-04-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000003||ur2biteme||09-04-2001||03:50 PM||||right on guys.  that's what i've been wanting to hear.  that's what i remember hearing as well.  i remember that it's a huge ordeal to bolt a pre-87 engine into an 87+, and vice versa, but not that the 87 engine is an exclusive part.  just kinda curious about v6 mounts.....||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||09-04-2001||08:32 PM||||The V6 mounts for the automatic trasnmission. Instead of the monomount it has now. Read the torque strut article in my cave to better understand the issue.||||reg||1
Z||000005||mrfiero||09-04-2001||08:38 PM||||His coupe's a 5-sp., so the mounts won't help him much (I sold him a replacement tranny, so I know  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ) <P>I still have that 80K mile '88 4-cyl. engine, so LMK if you decide you want it (unless you found something closer).<P>||||reg||1
